# serveros-evening-alignment.timer — the arm that makes the evening brief happen.
#
# SHIPPED FROM 2026-10-08, and until then it lived only on this node. Its two
# siblings that need no node fact — `serveros-alert-sync.timer` and
# `serveros-daily.timer` — had been in `runtime/` from the start; this one had
# not, so the argument below was durable as a file on one machine and invisible
# to every test, build and check this product runs. The template carries no
# placeholder: an hour and a zone are facts about the reader, and both are named
# here rather than supplied at install time.
#
# WHY 20:00 AND WHY THE GAP IS FORTY MINUTES
# ------------------------------------------
# 20:00 Asia/Shanghai, forty minutes after `serveros-intake.timer` fires at 19:20.
# The gap is not decoration: the intake run may take up to 900 s (that unit's own
# `TimeoutStartSec`), and `alignment.json` is put in place by `os.replace`
# (`intake/alignment_delivery.py:216`), so there is no half-written file to
# compose from. What firing too early produces is the PREVIOUS day's file, and
# `report evening` refuses it rather than composing: it compares the file's own
# mtime day against the brief's Beijing day and names both
# (`intake/alignment_delivery.py:612-620`, which states the reason — the recipient
# would get a card as calm as usual describing yesterday). So the failure mode of
# firing too early is a failed composition, not a wrong card.
#
# `serveros-intake.timer` is NOT part of this product and this repository does
# not carry it: two of its three ExecStart lines run scripts that live under
# `runtime-assets/` and belong to whatever owns them, and its third names one
# person's Feishu chat and one document URL. The 19:20 it fires at is therefore a
# fact this file states and cannot check. What it CAN do is refuse to be wrong
# about its own half, which the comment above is.
#
# WHY THE ZONE IS NAMED RATHER THAN INHERITED
# -------------------------------------------
# This host's system timezone is not the reader's, and a timer that fires at
# 20:00 UTC would be a card at 04:00.
#
# WHY Persistent=true HERE AND false ON THE WORK-BOARD TIMER
# ---------------------------------------------------------
# Catch up if the host was down at 20:00. The sibling `serveros-daily.timer`
# states the same reasoning at length: a missed composition is a day's brief that
# was never produced, so a catch-up produces it LATE rather than producing a
# burst of anything. `serveros-alert-sync` reaches the opposite answer because
# its queue is a register, and that difference is why this is stated rather than
# copied.

[Unit]
Description=每晚 20:00：把 19:20 的准备结果变成一份送得出去的当晚对齐

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 20:00:00 Asia/Shanghai
AccuracySec=1min
Persistent=true
Unit=serveros-evening-alignment.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
